@tradition windowsill-herbs
// Round 2: four people grow herbs on their windowsills for the galley; once a month they compare pots in the garden and the best bunch goes to Brennan. Every 4 weeks from week 6 (Days 36, 64...).
// Rules: FX24 (0.93.2, behind TRAD_0932_ON in section 13). Words: CS1 (plans/trad-0932-words.txt, claude/crew-stories-pitch 7b1e7300).
k: 1307
title: Windowsill herbs
when: every 4 weeks monday week 2 from day 36
at: 17:30-18:00
min: 20
after-shift: yes
where: 3 pool garden
who: janssen-hugo always, quist-ilse always, ishikawa-orla always, nakamura-bilal always, gardener 35%, garden-lover 30%, everyone 5%
anim: water
host: janssen-hugo
from: janssen-hugo
invite: host=janssen-hugo odds=25% line="Windowsill herbs in the garden. Bring a pot, or just a nose."

== mail
- Windowsill herbs tomorrow, {time}, in the garden. The windowsill growers bring their pots, swap cuttings, and the best bunch goes to Brennan. Come and sniff.

== ask
- Herb swap in the garden later. Hugo's mint is enormous.
- Windowsill herbs. Somebody's basil is going to the galley. Not mine.   #funny
- Do you grow anything on your windowsill? Bring it. They'll judge it nicely.

== here
- Smell that. That's rosemary that loves you.   #warm
- A cutting for a cutting. Fair.
- Whose thyme is this? It's very tidy.
- Brennan's coming to choose. Look busy.   #funny

== thanks
- The windowsill growers line up their pots in the garden, swap cuttings and argue gently about whose basil is best. The best bunch goes to the galley.

== chatter
- Hugo's mint won the windowsill herbs. Brennan took the lot.
- I swapped a cutting at the herb swap. Now I have a plant. Help.   #funny
- The garden smelled of basil all evening after the herb swap.
